at  kill viewers sound familiar and  installations that result in dozens of  casualties these anomalous art  terrorists are extremely dangerous and  no one knows them better than the  foundation chicago being known for its  art is one of their favorite haunts so  when the foundation launched a stakeout  operation tracking known are we cool yet  members they knew they'd find something  eventually that happened in june when  two foundation agents tailing a group of  are we cool yet members saw them moving  a number of paintings out of a truck and  into what seemed to be a regular  condominium the agents excited to  finally get a lead jumped out of the car  and quietly followed after them right  into the door of the building they  rushed in with their guns to find  nothing but on the second floor  things were more interesting one of the  are we cool yet members was laying on  the ground writhing in pain and covering  his face upon being poked by one of the  agents he lowered his hands revealing a  gory sight the man's face was warped  like a picasso painting his nose was on  his forehead his mouth was slanted all  the way to the left of his face and his  eyes were on his tongue he cries that  the gallery did this to him and that his  friend ran in the agents turn into the  bedroom instead of a wall and a window a  large hallway leading into a space that  doesn't exist outside the building is  present  scp-4149 the last thing the agents see  before calling for backup another are we  cool yet member shaking hands with what  appears to be a gigantic sloth in a  three-piece suit by the time the mtf  arrived with special anti-cognito hazard  gear they were all ready to enter  scp-4149  the four-man team enters rounding a  corner into what appears to be a  makeshift art gallery filled with  anthropomorphic animals lizards in  loungewear birds and fancy dresses and  the large sloth in a suit the agents had  seen along the walls are paintings and  artworks blurred by the agent's special  eyewear it doesn't take long before the  team are noticed by the animals  scp-4149 instances who start criticizing  their acting in english to the mtf's  surprise the heavily armed men start  hearing complaints in incompetent social  commentary about their lack of subtlety  from a growing crowd of clothed giant  animals confused they are eventually  rescued by the sloth who plays off their  strange arrival as a performance piece  gone awry and dismisses the crowd to  other art pieces after very slowly  dragging them into a corner the bested  sloth politely introduces himself as  professor zorkanov the owner of this art  gallery he claims to be a man of culture  and enjoyer of fine art who found he  could only truly operate his gallery how  he wanted free of the bounds of any one  world in fact the entirety of  scp-4149 exists in its own pocket  dimension upon being asked he explained  that the are we cool yet member was  trying to sell him some work but it  wasn't refined enough for the  professor's tastes but the artist seemed  to have run off to another planet to  train specifically one lacking an  atmosphere the professor agrees to be  designated as  scp-4149-2 and undergo interviewing to  help the foundation understand what the  situation surrounding his gallery is  which is where the foundation finds most  of their information for the anomalies  description  scp-4149 is what's known as an  extra-dimensional space a location that  doesn't quite exist in any one reality  but by itself in a pocket dimension it's  accessible through a hallway in the  apartment building which the foundation  has bought and slated for demolition  inside  scp-4149 one can access a large  warehouse serving as a gallery  containing upwards of 70 different art  pieces ranging from fancy oil paintings  to contemporary sculptures and modern  art almost all of them are cognito  hazardous in one way or another  extremely dangerous to the untrained  human mind the gallery itself seems to  be populated by a wide variety of  entities not just the finely dressed  animals that caught the mtf off guard  they claim to come from all the various  neighboring universes and realities that  scp-4149 borders and seemed to be fine  looking at all of the arc pieces and of  course the proprietor of the  establishment scp-4149-2  professor zorkonov 2 meters tall dressed  in a nice waistcoat and tweed jacket  foundation agents all describe him as  friendly and polite to a fault even if  he is a giant sloth unfortunately that  means everything he says or does is at a  snail's pace or more accurately a sloth  space but he usually spends his time  plodding between the various art pieces  and explaining or discussing them with  the guests as curator of the gallery  where the professor gets the artworks  isn't quite clear nor is how he says he  can travel through universes and worlds  to some degree but this is unconfirmed  for now all the foundation knows is that  sometimes the works in  scp-4149 just suddenly seem to cycle out  with new attractions the gallery isn't a  perfect socializing space though the  entry that exists in the apartment  building is a design flaw a construction  error but not one that can be easily  fixed without tearing the entire place  down and starting again something the  professor has sounded very upset at when  someone deciphered his glacial yelling  scp-4149 is friendly to foundation  interests though the professor doesn't  want uninvited guests to know about his  gallery any more than the foundation  does to that end he's cut a deal so long  as  scp-4149 submits to background  interviews and  scp-4149 is carefully kept under  containment  scp-4149-2 will be permitted to keep  operating his gallery and the foundation  will protect it against hostile  intruders what intruders you ask well  you'll have to look to the interviews  for that the main interview is conducted  by a d-class through an earpiece the  giant sloth statement have 